-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 10. DELFT ISLAND (NEDUNTHEEVU)
-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

CALL ict_insert_dest_if_missing(
    'Delft Island',
    'delft-island',
    'A remote, desolate island off the northern coast where wild horses roam, giant baobab trees grow, and fences are made of coral.',
    'Delft Island — known locally as Neduntheevu — sits in the Palk Strait, a two-hour ferry ride from Jaffna. It is a place apart. The landscape is flat, dry, and windswept, covered in palmyra palms and scrub. The soil is limestone, white and dusty. The fences are made of coral blocks. The roads are crushed coral. Wild horses — descendants of Arab and Portuguese horses brought to the island centuries ago — roam freely. Giant baobab trees, thousands of years old, stand sentinel over the empty plains. There are a few small villages, some colonial ruins, and almost no tourist infrastructure. Delft is not a comfortable destination. It is a raw, haunting, beautiful place that feels like the end of the earth.',
    'The wild horses are the most famous attraction — they roam the island free and are frankly stunning against the white soil and blue sky. The baobab trees are enormous and ancient. The coral fences are unique — a construction tradition found nowhere else in Sri Lanka. The ruins of a Dutch fort, a colonial rest house, and a temple add historical interest. The ferry ride across the Palk Strait is itself an experience on a clear day.',
    'Photograph the wild horses on the open plains. Visit the giant baobab trees (several are over 500 years old). Walk the coral fences lining the roads. Explore the Dutch fort ruins. Visit the old colonial rest house. See the ancient temple ruins. Take a bicycle or tuk-tuk tour of the island (3 hours to circumnavigate). Swim at the Casuarina Beach on the east side. Watch the local fishermen return with their catch.',
    'December to March is the best time — the weather is relatively cool and dry. April to October is extremely hot and windy. The ferry runs year-round but can be cancelled in rough seas. The island is exposed — there is almost no shade.',
    'From Jaffna town, drive to Kurikaduwan Jetty (30 minutes). Take the ferry to Delft Island (2 hours, runs twice daily at 6 AM and 10 AM approximately). Return ferries leave Delft at 5:30 AM and 2 PM. The ferry schedule is subject to change. Private boats can be arranged for groups.',
    'Delft is a day trip from Jaffna. The ferry schedule requires an early start. You will have about 4 hours on the island before the return ferry. A bicycle or tuk-tuk is essential to cover the island in that time.',
    'There is very limited accommodation on the island — basic guesthouses only. Most visitors stay in Jaffna and visit Delft as a day trip. Jetwing Jaffna or Fox Jaffna are the best bases.',
    'Take everything you need for the day — water, food, sunblock, a hat. There are very few shops on the island. The ferry is basic and can be rough. The horses are wild — do not feed or approach them too closely. The sun is brutal — take shelter during the middle of the day. A bicycle is the best way to see the island; tuk-tuks are available at the jetty.',
    '[{"q":"Is Delft Island worth the journey?","a":"For off-the-beaten-path travellers, yes. For anyone wanting a comfortable beach holiday, no. It is raw, remote, and unforgettable."},{"q":"Can I stay overnight on the island?","a":"Yes, but accommodation is very basic. Most visitors do a day trip from Jaffna."},{"q":"Are the wild horses dangerous?","a":"No. They are not aggressive but they are wild. Keep a respectful distance."}]',
    'Plan Your Delft Island Adventure',
    'We can organise your Delft Island day trip from Jaffna — ferry tickets, island transport, and a guide who knows where the baobabs and horses are.',
    'Northern Province',
    '30–38°C',
    'Remote Island',
    'Full day (day trip)',
    'Full day',
    'east',
    'East Coast',
    '🐴',
    50, 10, 5.5, 'De',
    'Delft Island Travel Guide | Island Culture Travels',
    'Discover Delft Island: wild horses, giant baobab trees, coral fences, Dutch ruins, and raw northern Sri Lankan beauty — a day trip from Jaffna.',
    59, 1, 1, 'Remote Island',
    'Wild horses, ancient baobabs, and coral fences on a remote northern island',
    'Jaffna, Nagadeepa, Kayts',
    'Jaffna: 30 min + 2 hr ferry. Point Pedro: 45 min + ferry. Colombo: 8 hrs.',
