-- 12. MEEMURE VILLAGE
-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

CALL ict_insert_dest_if_missing(
    'Meemure Village',
    'meemure',
    'A remote traditional village in the Knuckles foothills with crystal-clear rivers, jungle valleys, and authentic homestay experiences.',
    'Meemure is one of the most remote villages in Sri Lanka, nestled in a valley deep in the Knuckles Mountain Range. It is a living museum of traditional Sri Lankan village life. The houses are built from mud, wattle, and timber. The people grow paddy, spices, and vegetables on terraced slopes. The river that runs through the valley is clean enough to drink. There is no electricity grid — solar panels and kerosene lamps provide light. The road ends at a ridge; the last hour to reach Meemure is a hike through the forest. It is not comfortable. There is no luxury. But for travellers seeking authentic rural life, the experience of staying in a Meemure homestay — eating rice and curry cooked on a wood fire, sleeping on a mat, falling asleep to the sound of the river — is unforgettable.',
    'The setting is stunning. The valley is surrounded by the peaks of the Knuckles range. The river has deep pools for swimming and waterfalls for bathing. The rice terraces are carved into the hillsides. The homestay experience is genuinely authentic — you eat with the family, help with farming tasks, and learn about traditional agriculture. The hike to Meemure itself is a beautiful walk through the forest. At night, with no electricity, the stars are incredible.',
    'Walk the final leg into the village (1 hour hike from the road). Stay in a traditional homestay (no alternatives). Swim in the river pools. Hike to the nearby waterfalls. Walk through the paddy terraces. Learn traditional farming from your hosts. Help prepare a wood-fire rice and curry. Stargaze at night — there is no light pollution. Hike to the Knuckles peaks from Meemure (advanced, multi-day). Visit the nearby village of Kottegoda.',
    'January to April is the dry season — the river is safe for swimming and the trails are dry. May to July brings rain and the river can swell dangerously. August to September is a second dry window. October to December is wet.',
    'About 130 kilometres from Colombo — 4 hours by car to the trailhead via Kandy and Thelgamuwa. The last 20 km are on rough, winding roads suitable only for 4WD. From Thelgamuwa, the road to the Meemure trailhead is a rutted track. From there it is a 1-hour hike into the village. Public transport goes as far as Kandy; from there you need private 4WD.',
    'Minimum two nights — the travel time means one night is too rushed. Day one: drive from Kandy, hike in, settle in. Day two: explore the valley, river swim, village walk. Day three: morning hike out. Three nights is better for deeper immersion.',
    'Homestays only. The village has several families who host guests. The accommodation is basic: a room with a mat, a shared toilet, and meals on a veranda. The experience is the point. Book through a local guide from Kandy who knows the families.',
    'This is not a luxury destination. You will sleep on a mat, eat simple food, and use a basic toilet. Take a sleeping bag liner, a torch, and insect repellent. The hike in is moderately strenuous — pack light. The river water is safe to drink but treat it if you are cautious. Respect the village customs: dress modestly, ask before photographing people. Mobile reception is available at points on the ridge but not in the valley.',
    '[{"q":"Is Meemure suitable for children?","a":"Older children who can manage the hike will love the adventure. Very young children may struggle with the walk."},{"q":"What should I bring to Meemure?","a":"A torch, sleeping bag liner, insect repellent, and a book. Pack light — you carry everything in."},{"q":"Is the hike to Meemure difficult?","a":"Moderate. The trail is downhill on the way in and uphill on the way out. Allow 1 hour each way."}]',
    'Plan Your Meemure Village Homestay Experience',
    'We can arrange a traditional homestay in Meemure village, including 4WD transport, guided hike, and all meals with a local family.',
    'Central Province',
    '18–26°C',
    'Rural / Homestay',
    '2–3 Days',
    '2–3 days',
    'hill',
    'Hill Country',
    '🏡',
    117, 180, 5.0, 'Me',
    'Meemure Village Homestay Guide | Island Culture Travels',
    'Plan a Meemure village experience: remote homestay in the Knuckles foothills, river treks, traditional farming, wood-fire rice and curry, and stargazing.',
    61, 1, 1, 'Rural / Homestay',
    'A remote traditional village in the Knuckles foothills with authentic homestays',
    'Kandy, Knuckles Mountain Range, Matale',
    'Kandy: 3 hrs. Thelgamuwa: 1 hr. Knuckles: 30 min hike from trailhead. Colombo: 5 hrs.',
    '{"months":[{"month":"Jan","rating":"great"},{"month":"Feb","rating":"great"},{"month":"Mar","rating":"great"},{"month":"Apr","rating":"great"},{"month":"May","rating":"avoid"},{"month":"Jun","rating":"avoid"},{"month":"Jul","rating":"avoid"},{"month":"Aug","rating":"okay"},{"month":"Sep","rating":"okay"},{"month":"Oct","rating":"avoid"},{"month":"Nov","rating":"avoid"},{"month":"Dec","rating":"avoid"}],"note":"Jan-Apr is the best time. Rivers are clearest and trails are driest."}',
    'Jan–Apr',
    'Aug–Sep',
    'May–Jul, Oct–Dec',
    'Cool and clear. Rivers safest in the dry season (Jan-Apr).',
    'Jan',
    'Apr',
    '{"nationalities":["GER","UK","AUS"],"top_activities":["River trekking","Village homestays","Traditional cooking","Stargazing","Waterfall hikes"],"traveler_types":["adventure","solo","eco","culture"]}',
    '[{"platform":"TripAdvisor","score":"5.0","url":"","notes":"Niche — life-changing experience for adventurous travellers"},{"platform":"Booking.com","score":"9.0","url":"","notes":"Homestays rated highly by guests"}]',
    'Challenging',
    '4x4 + Hike',
    'Very Quiet',
    'Logistical Effort: Requires a 4x4 and a 1-hour hike to reach the village. The Catch: No luxury; basic amenities. For authentic cultural immersion only. The hike is moderately strenuous.',
    '[{"name":"Knuckles Peak","type":"mountain","distance":"hike from village"},{"name":"Bambarakiri Ella","type":"waterfall","distance":"walking distance"},{"name":"Kottegoda Village","type":"village","distance":"1 hr walk"}]',
    '[{"slug":"knuckles-mountain-range","why":"Extend into a multi-day Knuckles trek from a Meemure base"},{"slug":"kandy","why":"Start or end your Meemure journey at Sri Lanka\'s cultural capital"},{"slug":"matale","why":"Stop at the spice gardens on the route from Kandy"}]'
